    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\n`Gemma4ToolUtils.tool_extractor` converts the Gemma 4 call syntax to JSON in two regex passes: first `<|\"|>...<|\"|>` becomes a JSON string, then every bare identifier followed by `:` gets quoted. The second pass also runs inside the strings produced by the first one, so a string argument such as `Hi Tom, Re: the plan` becomes `\"Hi Tom, \"Re\": the plan\"`. `json.loads` then fails and the extractor returns the raw text as the arguments string.\n\nThis also means `function_formatter` output does not round-trip:\n\n    <|tool_call>call:f{text:<|\"|>Dear John, Re: the meeting<|\"|>}<tool_call|>\n    -> FunctionCall(name='f', arguments='text:<|\"|>Dear John, Re: the meeting<|\"|>')\n\nThe fix does both steps in one left-to-right `re.sub` with alternation. A whole `<|\"|>...<|\"|>` string is matched first, so its content is never treated as a key. Key quoting outside strings is unchanged.\n\nTests: `test_gemma4_tool_extractor_colon_in_string` and `test_gemma4_tool_round_trip` in `tests/data/test_formatter.py`. Both fail on main with `JSONDecodeError` and pass with this change. `tests/data/test_formatter.py`: 48 passed. `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` are clean.\n\nFixes # (no issue filed)\n\nAI assistance: I used Claude Code to help find the bug and draft the patch and tests. I reviewed and ran everything myself.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
